      "facts": [
        "Mirrors the SDK: a provider-executed call needs no local result, so tracking one would defer every later image forever.",
        "Anything still buffered had no clean boundary; dropUnansweredToolCalls has already removed calls that never get answered, so this is just a backstop."
      ],
      "title": "Shared/Core update: messages",
      "summary": "Shared/Core, SDK changes across 1 file(s) (+296/−1).",
      "tags": [
        "sdk"
      ],
      "day": "2026-08-15",
      "month": "2026-08",
      "category": "SDK",
      "significance": "minor",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Buffer media until tool calls answered in messages.ts",
        "summary": "convertToolMessages now buffers media parts until all tool calls are answered, preventing AI SDK validation errors when parallel calls are interleaved with media. The logic tracks unanswered toolCallIds, skipping provider-executed calls, and flushes pending media only when the set is empty. This fixes threads wedging during history replay where media inline split batches. Implemented in common/src/util/messages.ts as a backstop alongside dropUnansweredToolCalls.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T05:11:02.547Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you ask the assistant to do several things at once that involve photos or images, your app used to freeze up while it waited for all the answers to come back. Now the program keeps those photos in line instead of letting them spill out between the separate answers, which is what was tripping up the validation and getting threads stuck when your conversation history was replayed. You don't tap any new button or setting for it: the next time a multi-step request with images gets answered, it simply completes instead of locking up.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "60e2e9d8d0d9",
        "at": "2026-09-17T20:10:59.478Z"
